WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.850 --> 00:00:07.960
Hello.

00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:11.770
I'm Eran Egozy, class of '95 and
Professor of Music Technology

00:00:11.770 --> 00:00:13.240
here at MIT.

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:16.059
You're about to hear a piece
of music composed specifically

00:00:16.059 --> 00:00:17.530
for today's commencement.

00:00:17.530 --> 00:00:19.180
But there is a twist.

00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:22.360
We asked the MIT community,
and in particular, this year's

00:00:22.360 --> 00:00:25.600
graduates, to sing
a single note and be

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:30.300
part of a collective experience
that we are calling comusica.

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:32.820
We received over
800 contributions.

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:35.520
And then our amazing
team of MIT coders,

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:37.680
videographers, and
sound designers,

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:40.410
stitched them all together
into a collaborative work that

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:43.470
celebrates our graduating
students coming together

00:00:43.470 --> 00:00:45.450
as one MIT.

00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:46.440
I hope you enjoy it.

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:58.190
[MUSIC PLAYING]

